{title: Make His Face Shine Upon Us}
{subtitle: Psalms 67:1–2}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 95}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Ab] | [Ab] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
May God [Eb]be gracious to us and bless [Cm]us
And make his [Ab]face shine upon [Eb]us
His light [Cm]breaks through the morn[Bb]ing
A mer[Ab]cy that we cannot [Bb]earn
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Let your way be known on earth
[Cm]Your salvation among all nations
[Ab]Let the peoples praise you, [Bb]O God
[Ab]Let all the peo[Bb]ples praise you [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The nations are glad and sing for [Cm]joy
For you [Ab]judge the peoples with fairness
You guide [Cm]them upon the [Bb]earth
A path [Ab]of justice and [Bb]grace
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Your hand reaches [Bb]out to all
[Cm]No boundary [Eb]holds your love
[Ab]The world turns to [Bb]see your light
And [Cm]bows before [Bb/D]your [Eb][Ab]throne
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
May God [Eb]be gracious to us and bless [Cm]us
And make his [Ab]face shine upon [Eb]us
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Ab] | [Bb] | [Ab] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Ab] | [Ab] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
